---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="The Melodica — Panache"
  description="You found it. A hidden corner of Panache history."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="kicker">You found the secret</p>
    <h1>The Melodica</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      If you're here, you either guessed very well or you read the archive
      carefully enough to remember Archie Petrie and the 2D Sparklers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap prose">
    <p>
      Before Panache, before Auricle, before even the Violent Sabbath and the
      Slug Band, there was a school band at Greenock High called the 2D
      Sparklers. Archie Petrie played melodica.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's a small detail in a long history, but it's the kind of thing that
      matters when you're trying to piece together how five musicians from
      Inverclyde became Scotland's answer to Steely Dan.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page has no links pointing to it. The sitemap doesn't list it.
      Navigation skips over it. You had to know to look.
    </p>
    <p>
      Thank you for caring enough to find it.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>For the archivists</h2>
    <p>
      If you played in one of these bands — the 2D Sparklers, Violent Sabbath,
      the Slug Band, Auricle, or Panache itself — or if you photographed them,
      recorded them, or have tapes, setlists, posters, or memories, please write.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're trying to recover as much of this story as we can, tape by tape,
      detail by detail.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:info@panachetheband.com">info@panachetheband.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
